1
00:00:11,320 --> 00:00:17,540
Toward the setting sun
floating over the Nakagawa,

2
00:00:18,060 --> 00:00:24,660
I kick a pebble and even my shoes fly off.

3
00:00:24,660 --> 00:00:32,960
Onto the head of a
carpenter who was jogging,

4
00:00:32,960 --> 00:00:39,140
they laughed that I'm still just a kid.

5
00:00:39,760 --> 00:00:44,220
Even if I somehow summon some energy,

6
00:00:44,220 --> 00:00:49,280
bright-eyed, sighing,
one more yawn, nothing changes.

7
00:00:49,280 --> 00:00:53,180
The streets look oddly gentle.

8
00:00:54,660 --> 00:01:01,140
From the pointed-hat water basin,

9
00:01:01,720 --> 00:01:07,440
the sun sinks into the great sky.

10
00:01:11,020 --> 00:01:15,920
Tomorrow too, it'll end just like this

11
00:01:15,920 --> 00:01:21,060
Katsushika, Shibamata,
even happiness is lost again,

12
00:01:22,060 --> 00:01:24,680
because I'm just a foolish
guy who got carried away.

13
00:01:29,380 --> 00:01:31,920
Pursuit! Ryotsu!

14
00:01:37,460 --> 00:01:41,060
Headquarters spent a billion
yen raising and training it.

15
00:01:41,060 --> 00:01:43,900
High-tech police dog, Bergmann.

16
00:01:48,700 --> 00:01:51,220
You two, go ahead and explain it to them.

17
00:01:52,600 --> 00:01:55,200
Well then, in Germany,
where police dog training is top-notch,

18
00:01:55,560 --> 00:02:00,040
let's see for ourselves the abilities of a dog
that graduated first after four years of training.

19
00:02:08,640 --> 00:02:12,560
A stolen wallet has been planted in
advance in one of these men's clothes.

20
00:02:13,320 --> 00:02:15,600
Now, Bergmann, arrest the culprit!

21
00:02:20,800 --> 00:02:22,200
It shook its head.

22
00:02:22,200 --> 00:02:24,080
So none of them is the culprit?

23
00:02:24,080 --> 00:02:25,400
Wanna go?

24
00:02:28,680 --> 00:02:30,100
Looks like it's the wrong one again.

25
00:02:30,100 --> 00:02:31,560
So then the culprit would be...

26
00:02:37,840 --> 00:02:40,700
This mutt thinks he can mad-dog
me just 'cause he's a dog!

27
00:02:51,740 --> 00:02:53,840
No matter what happens,

28
00:02:54,240 --> 00:02:56,820
Bergmann is trained never
to let the criminal escape.

29
00:02:58,240 --> 00:03:00,800
With the tracking camera
attached to Bergmann,

30
00:03:00,800 --> 00:03:02,260
let's watch the arrest.

31
00:03:06,160 --> 00:03:06,800
This is amazing.

32
00:03:06,800 --> 00:03:09,900
It's like we're actually
chasing him ourselves.

33
00:03:12,240 --> 00:03:14,820
The criminal's face and
the progress of the chase

34
00:03:14,820 --> 00:03:18,240
are all recorded step by step,
becoming strong evidence for trials.

35
00:03:18,240 --> 00:03:20,620
Communication through a
microphone is also possible.

36
00:03:21,660 --> 00:03:23,220
Voices can be recorded as well.

37
00:03:23,680 --> 00:03:24,400
Fast!

38
00:03:24,900 --> 00:03:27,620
Bergmann's speed is on par with a car.

39
00:03:30,780 --> 00:03:33,280
Super jumping power that
clears 5-meter walls.

40
00:03:36,380 --> 00:03:38,720
Damn it! What a persistent dog!

41
00:03:38,880 --> 00:03:40,120
Whoa! Watch out, that's dangerous!

42
00:03:43,320 --> 00:03:45,580
Bergmann fears nothing,
not even going into a stomach.

43
00:03:46,480 --> 00:03:46,840
Incredible!

44
00:03:47,760 --> 00:03:49,100
Yowch, yowch, yowch!

45
00:03:53,540 --> 00:03:57,240
Swimming is his specialty of specialties.

46
00:04:05,660 --> 00:04:07,260
Stop! Now it's a showdown!

47
00:04:20,960 --> 00:04:21,620
Here it comes!

48
00:04:22,200 --> 00:04:23,640
Bergmann's signature move!

49
00:04:23,880 --> 00:04:25,560
Moonsault attack!

50
00:04:30,360 --> 00:04:31,160
Let go!

51
00:04:31,400 --> 00:04:32,040
Hey!

52
00:04:34,720 --> 00:04:36,100
Let go! Let go!

53
00:04:37,360 --> 00:04:39,260
Let go! Let go!

54
00:04:39,820 --> 00:04:42,020
I give up! Have mercy!

55
00:04:45,100 --> 00:04:48,425
As you can see, it perfectly picked
out the culprit from the three men,

56
00:04:48,475 --> 00:04:49,600
and made the arrest.

57
00:04:49,840 --> 00:04:52,280
There's no escaping this Bergmann!

58
00:04:52,740 --> 00:04:54,940
Yes, it really is an amazing dog.

59
00:04:55,260 --> 00:04:58,580
After all, we spent a full billion yen on it,
a billion yen.

60
00:04:58,580 --> 00:05:03,540
It's an honor that our Katsushika station
was chosen for this dog's field training.

61
00:05:03,540 --> 00:05:08,100
So we'd like to choose Bergmann's
partner for this training.

62
00:05:08,100 --> 00:05:09,900
Please choose whoever you like.

63
00:05:10,300 --> 00:05:15,540
Our station has many talented officers we can be proud of,
even compared to headquarters.

64
00:05:15,540 --> 00:05:15,960
Yes.

65
00:05:16,340 --> 00:05:19,699
We've already entered the
grades and personalities

66
00:05:19,749 --> 00:05:22,520
of every Katsushika officer, along with
blood types, horoscope signs, nicknames,

67
00:05:22,520 --> 00:05:24,780
and everything else into the computer.

68
00:05:25,540 --> 00:05:29,060
The computer will choose the
partner best suited for Bergmann.

69
00:05:30,180 --> 00:05:31,620
I see, that's very rational.

70
00:05:31,620 --> 00:05:32,840
Well then, here we go.

71
00:05:38,900 --> 00:05:42,260
Who's the poor soul stuck
being this dog's partner?

72
00:05:47,140 --> 00:05:47,980
It's been decided.

73
00:05:48,420 --> 00:05:50,960
Bergmann's partner is this man.

74
00:05:52,300 --> 00:05:54,080
Senior Constable Kankichi Ryotsu.

75
00:05:58,960 --> 00:06:00,640
Why of all people does it have to be Ryotsu?

76
00:06:00,640 --> 00:06:02,180
This must be some kind of mistake.

77
00:06:02,180 --> 00:06:02,620
Congratulations.

78
00:06:02,620 --> 00:06:05,780
This is truly an honor.

79
00:06:06,920 --> 00:06:08,540
No, do your best, won't you?

80
00:06:08,540 --> 00:06:11,960
The future of Japan rests on your research.

81
00:06:14,640 --> 00:06:16,380
Well, there's nothing more to say after that,
is there.

82
00:06:16,380 --> 00:06:17,520
Honestly.

83
00:06:18,980 --> 00:06:20,940
Japan's first police dog and his partner.

84
00:06:20,940 --> 00:06:22,520
Senior Constable Ryotsu, reporting for duty!

85
00:06:23,760 --> 00:06:24,120
Well then,

86
00:06:24,540 --> 00:06:25,740
starting today, for two weeks.

87
00:06:25,740 --> 00:06:27,780
I'm entrusting Bergmann to you.

88
00:06:28,800 --> 00:06:31,260
This is Bergmann's daily schedule.

89
00:06:31,880 --> 00:06:32,760
What the heck is this?

90
00:06:33,760 --> 00:06:36,320
Does this mutt live a more disciplined life than a human,
or what?

91
00:06:36,740 --> 00:06:37,640
Listen, Ryotsu.

92
00:06:38,020 --> 00:06:40,040
This dog cost a billion yen, you know.

93
00:06:40,040 --> 00:06:42,340
Whatever you do, don't cause any trouble.

94
00:06:42,340 --> 00:06:44,260
Yeah, yeah, I get it.

95
00:06:44,260 --> 00:06:46,180
It's just one or two dogs.

96
00:06:47,440 --> 00:06:49,260
Hey, what on earth is wrong with you?

97
00:06:49,940 --> 00:06:51,060
It's 4 p.m. now.

98
00:06:51,060 --> 00:06:53,260
It's Bergmann's running time.

99
00:06:53,260 --> 00:06:54,840
Hey, stop running now.

100
00:06:55,280 --> 00:06:58,320
I hope nothing goes wrong with Ryotsu.

101
00:06:58,320 --> 00:06:59,320
Honestly.

102
00:07:00,120 --> 00:07:01,780
Hey, how long are you going to keep running?

103
00:07:04,760 --> 00:07:06,540
Woah, woah!

104
00:07:06,540 --> 00:07:07,260
Shh!

105
00:07:07,260 --> 00:07:09,380
Shh!

106
00:07:09,380 --> 00:07:10,580
Haa...

107
00:07:10,580 --> 00:07:12,740
Haa...

108
00:07:12,740 --> 00:07:12,860
Haa...

109
00:07:12,860 --> 00:07:14,160
Haa...

110
00:07:14,160 --> 00:07:14,400
Haa...

111
00:07:14,400 --> 00:07:15,700
Haa...

112
00:07:15,700 --> 00:07:15,740
Haa...

113
00:07:15,740 --> 00:07:16,140
Haa...

114
00:07:16,140 --> 00:07:16,520
Haa...

115
00:07:16,520 --> 00:07:16,740
Haa...

116
00:07:16,740 --> 00:07:17,660
Haa...

117
00:07:26,200 --> 00:07:27,160
That hurts.

118
00:07:32,760 --> 00:07:34,220
What a clever guy.

119
00:07:43,000 --> 00:07:45,360
Good morning. It's seven o'clock.

120
00:07:46,100 --> 00:07:48,440
Depending on the weather
and where we're headed,

121
00:07:52,340 --> 00:07:54,720
don't go running over there
first thing in the morning.

122
00:07:56,800 --> 00:07:58,760
Ryo-chan, you're up early!

123
00:07:58,760 --> 00:08:00,440
Good morning, senpai.

124
00:08:01,140 --> 00:08:05,040
Man, it's radio calisthenics and
running right from the crack of dawn!

125
00:08:05,040 --> 00:08:06,120
Ugh, what a pain.

126
00:08:06,120 --> 00:08:08,480
Honestly, I turned off my own alarm clock.

127
00:08:08,480 --> 00:08:11,100
I washed my face and brushed my teeth.

128
00:08:11,100 --> 00:08:13,160
What's all this?

129
00:08:14,440 --> 00:08:17,220
It's the monitor for
Bergmann's tracking camera.

130
00:08:18,440 --> 00:08:20,600
It's a small version of the
one you two were watching.

131
00:08:20,600 --> 00:08:22,380
From Bergmann's camera,

132
00:08:22,380 --> 00:08:24,160
footage within a two-kilometer radius

133
00:08:24,160 --> 00:08:25,880
can now be monitored.

134
00:08:25,880 --> 00:08:27,860
Reiko's on the screen!

135
00:08:27,860 --> 00:08:29,440
Wow, that's amazing.

136
00:08:33,260 --> 00:08:35,300
Using this one's tracking camera,

137
00:08:35,300 --> 00:08:36,920
let's have a little fun.

138
00:08:46,240 --> 00:08:48,260
Just a little peek at the ladies.

139
00:08:48,440 --> 00:08:49,360
Do as I say.

140
00:08:51,900 --> 00:08:54,820
No wonder,
after being trained in Germany and Japan.

141
00:08:54,820 --> 00:08:56,120
You're so stubborn, aren't you.

142
00:08:56,680 --> 00:09:00,880
And I was just planning to
have a beer with some snacks.

143
00:09:01,720 --> 00:09:03,860
Elite or not, your Japanese is still shaky.

144
00:09:10,420 --> 00:09:12,840
What, you want this beer?

145
00:09:13,400 --> 00:09:13,920
Let's see.

146
00:09:16,380 --> 00:09:18,240
What, you like beer?

147
00:09:19,600 --> 00:09:21,400
Alright, alright, drink up!

148
00:09:25,980 --> 00:09:28,080
Keep pouring him more, I say!

149
00:09:30,080 --> 00:09:32,080
Even people, the more elite they are,

150
00:09:32,080 --> 00:09:34,000
their personalities
change when they get drunk.

151
00:09:34,000 --> 00:09:35,480
You're that type too

152
00:09:40,420 --> 00:09:41,960
Maybe this one...

153
00:09:41,960 --> 00:09:44,740
If we get him really drunk,
he might actually listen.

154
00:09:45,800 --> 00:09:46,200
Alright.

155
00:09:47,140 --> 00:09:48,860
Come on, drink up, drink up!

156
00:09:52,200 --> 00:09:53,680
Yeah, that's it, Bergmann!

157
00:09:53,680 --> 00:09:55,020
Go on, go on!

158
00:10:03,420 --> 00:10:04,440
We did it!

159
00:10:05,440 --> 00:10:08,180
Make sure you record it.
It's a permanent keepsake.

160
00:10:10,440 --> 00:10:11,500
What's he on about?

161
00:10:12,060 --> 00:10:13,140
Damn! We've been spotted!

162
00:10:25,360 --> 00:10:27,440
Idiot! Don't make a bigger fuss!

163
00:10:32,560 --> 00:10:34,960
Bergmann! Come back! Bergmann!

164
00:10:36,160 --> 00:10:37,000
Crap!

165
00:10:37,120 --> 00:10:37,940
What do you think you're doing!

166
00:10:38,920 --> 00:10:42,300
No, well, this officer isn't one to talk much,
so please, go on patrol!

167
00:10:47,920 --> 00:10:48,940
It's too close!

168
00:10:49,120 --> 00:10:49,720
Over there!

169
00:10:49,900 --> 00:10:50,620
It's too close!

170
00:10:51,200 --> 00:10:52,100
R-really?!

171
00:11:01,400 --> 00:11:02,940
We got him drinking a bit too much.

172
00:11:02,940 --> 00:11:04,680
He's definitely going to have a hangover.

173
00:11:04,680 --> 00:11:05,840
This is a real problem.

174
00:11:05,840 --> 00:11:07,840
Honestly, what an outrageous story.

175
00:11:07,840 --> 00:11:09,100
Seriously, that's the worst.

176
00:11:09,100 --> 00:11:10,980
Ryotsu!

177
00:11:10,980 --> 00:11:13,800
Good morning, Chief!

178
00:11:14,980 --> 00:11:18,060
Is Bergmann feeling unwell or something?

179
00:11:18,060 --> 00:11:19,440
Not at all!

180
00:11:19,440 --> 00:11:21,520
See? Full of energy!

181
00:11:22,100 --> 00:11:24,980
I see. In that case, let's have him
start on an investigation right away.

182
00:11:25,200 --> 00:11:26,740
What investigation?

183
00:11:27,260 --> 00:11:28,596
Last night, using the dog,

184
00:11:28,646 --> 00:11:31,420
there was someone who tried
to peep into the women's bath.

185
00:11:31,720 --> 00:11:32,080
Gulp.

186
00:11:32,880 --> 00:11:35,880
How despicable.
Using a dog like that, I can't forgive it.

187
00:11:36,140 --> 00:11:38,157
Y-yeah, that's right. Exactly.

188
00:11:38,207 --> 00:11:40,620
You're a real lowlife, Bergmann.

189
00:11:41,600 --> 00:11:44,640
Bergmann says he won't
forgive a guy like that.

190
00:11:45,020 --> 00:11:48,780
So, this is the evidence
the culprit left behind.

191
00:11:50,520 --> 00:11:51,240
Gikugiku.

192
00:11:52,400 --> 00:11:54,841
Relying on the scent left on this empty can,

193
00:11:54,891 --> 00:11:57,660
I'm going to have Bergmann
track down the culprit.

194
00:11:57,740 --> 00:11:58,580
Got it!

195
00:11:59,020 --> 00:12:01,400
Come on, Bergmann,
this is the culprit's scent.

196
00:12:02,000 --> 00:12:04,180
Hey, hey,
can he really tell from that little bit?

197
00:12:04,360 --> 00:12:07,100
Well, after all, he's a ¥1 billion dog.

198
00:12:07,540 --> 00:12:09,600
Alright, go on, Bergmann!

199
00:12:14,100 --> 00:12:15,580
What's the matter?

200
00:12:16,260 --> 00:12:19,500
Look, it's completely taken
to me and playing the fool.

201
00:12:20,020 --> 00:12:22,520
Come on, Bergma. Work, work.

202
00:12:22,680 --> 00:12:26,400
What, what? I see. So you've figured
out which direction the culprit is in?

203
00:12:26,440 --> 00:12:27,807
Chief, Officer Ryotsu,

204
00:12:27,857 --> 00:12:30,820
we're heading out to investigate
the culprit with Bergmann.

205
00:12:31,460 --> 00:12:35,320
Right. We'll be watching the monitor here,
so do your best.

206
00:12:36,860 --> 00:12:40,200
Ryotsu,
make sure you don't get in Bergmann's way.

207
00:12:40,760 --> 00:12:42,460
Tch, understood.

208
00:13:01,120 --> 00:13:02,340
This is a real pain.

209
00:13:03,240 --> 00:13:05,660
Bergmann's hungover, so he's like this.

210
00:13:05,660 --> 00:13:07,140
How do I get the rubber out?

211
00:13:08,380 --> 00:13:09,440
Hey, Ryotsu.

212
00:13:09,840 --> 00:13:11,420
What are you muttering about?

213
00:13:11,980 --> 00:13:13,260
Can't you be serious?

214
00:13:14,180 --> 00:13:16,180
I can't even raise my voice carelessly.

215
00:13:20,360 --> 00:13:21,020
Uh-oh, crap.

216
00:13:21,020 --> 00:13:23,640
That guy's face looks familiar.

217
00:13:27,520 --> 00:13:28,380
This man...

218
00:13:32,680 --> 00:13:35,060
There he is, this is the man!

219
00:13:35,600 --> 00:13:39,540
The nationwide wanted thief,
the phantom thief Henno No. 56.

220
00:13:39,540 --> 00:13:41,120
Just as I thought.

221
00:13:41,680 --> 00:13:46,620
Ryotsu, that man is the nationwide
wanted phantom thief Henno No. 56!

222
00:13:46,620 --> 00:13:47,760
So it's this guy!

223
00:13:47,760 --> 00:13:48,600
Hold it!

224
00:13:51,380 --> 00:13:53,080
I forgot about Bergmann!

225
00:13:53,660 --> 00:13:56,160
Hey, wake up already!

226
00:13:56,160 --> 00:13:58,020
This guy's just getting in the way,
isn't he?

227
00:13:59,440 --> 00:14:01,300
Ryo-chan was making a racket or something.

228
00:14:01,740 --> 00:14:03,540
He's quite different from yesterday,
isn't he?

229
00:14:03,540 --> 00:14:05,240
Bergmann's speed is...

230
00:14:05,240 --> 00:14:06,900
And his eyes are all glazed over.

231
00:14:07,280 --> 00:14:08,120
Hey, Ryotsu!

232
00:14:08,120 --> 00:14:09,820
What happened to Bergmann?

233
00:14:09,820 --> 00:14:11,160
Did something happen?

234
00:14:11,160 --> 00:14:13,020
No, it's nothing.

235
00:14:13,740 --> 00:14:14,460
It's fine.

236
00:14:19,600 --> 00:14:20,620
That bastard!

237
00:14:22,100 --> 00:14:23,880
Hey, jump, Bergmann!

238
00:14:24,620 --> 00:14:25,820
There's no way he could

239
00:14:26,160 --> 00:14:27,180
...right?

240
00:14:27,180 --> 00:14:29,140
Where'd he go?

241
00:14:33,520 --> 00:14:33,940
What?

242
00:14:36,200 --> 00:14:37,340
Hey, are you okay?

243
00:14:37,560 --> 00:14:39,720
Yeah, snap out of it, Bergmann!

244
00:14:42,800 --> 00:14:45,360
He's as heavy as a stuffed toy.

245
00:14:47,320 --> 00:14:48,840
That's some strange movement, isn't it?

246
00:14:48,840 --> 00:14:50,700
Yeah, that's weird.

247
00:14:53,520 --> 00:14:55,100
Damn, stairs!

248
00:14:56,160 --> 00:14:58,760
Alright, let's go!

249
00:14:59,840 --> 00:15:00,640
He's heavy!

250
00:15:12,660 --> 00:15:14,160
Hey, move, move, move, move!

251
00:15:15,160 --> 00:15:16,320
He's going to get away!

252
00:15:16,520 --> 00:15:19,020
Go! Charge! Bergmann!

253
00:15:22,600 --> 00:15:24,020
Whoa, what a jump!

254
00:15:28,900 --> 00:15:30,100
Yes, we did it!

255
00:15:30,640 --> 00:15:33,600
So you're finally awake?

256
00:15:33,600 --> 00:15:36,220
Alright, Bergmann, arrest the culprit!

257
00:15:44,540 --> 00:15:47,420
Hey, wait! Don't get excited, calm down!

258
00:15:47,420 --> 00:15:48,560
Nooo!

259
00:15:48,560 --> 00:15:58,920


260
00:15:59,380 --> 00:16:00,460
What happened?

261
00:16:00,460 --> 00:16:02,860
Nothing, nothing at all.

262
00:16:04,540 --> 00:16:05,020
Run!

263
00:16:05,020 --> 00:16:06,800
Stop, you bastard!

264
00:16:06,800 --> 00:16:07,420
Damn it!

265
00:16:08,700 --> 00:16:11,900
If it comes to this, I'll have to
do it myself instead of Bergmann.

266
00:16:21,480 --> 00:16:22,920
This is tough.

267
